        "original_id": "1736d1b9-ac4a-5807-93f0-a396cfff5d6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Boomerang, Cartoon Network, Scooby-Doo, Looney Tunes, Tom and Jerry, Sonic Boom, The Powerpuff Girls, The Magilla Gorilla Show\n- Companies: Time Warner, Turner, Hanna-Barbera Productions\n- People: Joe Ruby, Ken Spears\n- Topics: Animated programming, cartoon franchise\n\nFacts:\n- Scooby-Doo was created for Hanna-Barbera Productions by writers Joe Ruby and Ken Spears in 1969.\n- Scooby-Doo is an American animated cartoon franchise comprising several animated television series produced from 1969 to the present day.\n- Boomerang specializes in classic and contemporary animated programming from Time Warner's archive, including Looney Tunes, Tom and Jerry, and Scooby-Doo.\n- Boomerang also airs repeats of in-production series from its sister and fellow Turner-owned channel Cartoon Network, including Sonic Boom and The Powerpuff Girls.\n- The Magilla Gorilla Show aired on Boomerang until July 22, 2012.",
